alwaysApply: true
---
Project: Mehar for Eyes, a showcase website for an established optical business in Pakistan. Not ecommerce yet. All orders happen via WhatsApp. Ecommerce will be added later, so keep product data separate from UI.

Stack: Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, next/image. No UI component libraries unless I ask. Backend will be a separate Go service in /backend (chi, pgx, sqlc, golang-migrate, Postgres), built later.

Design rules:
- Warm off-white background (#FAF7F2), near-black text (#1A1A1A), one accent color (#5A2E1F). No gradients, no glassmorphism, no purple/blue.
- Fonts via next/font: Fraunces (headings), DM Sans (body).
- Generous whitespace, large product imagery, hairline borders (1px), subtle motion only (fade/translate on scroll, 200-300ms).
- No emojis in UI. No lorem ipsum. No generic marketing copy like "Welcome to" or "Discover the best". Write short, specific, human copy.
- Mobile first. Must look correct at 360px width.
- Accessible: alt text on all images, visible focus states, contrast AA.
- Performance: all images through next/image with sizes, lazy load below the fold.

Data rules:
- For now, products come only from /data/products.ts, a dev stub. UI never hardcodes product info. All data access goes through functions in /lib/products.ts so the source can be swapped to the Go API later without touching components.
- Placeholder images live in /public/placeholders. Never hotlink external image URLs.
- WhatsApp link logic lives only in /lib/whatsapp.ts.

Code rules:
- Give full files, not snippets.